records.rationale:
In `app/assets/javascripts/discourse/models/group.js`, both `removeMember` and `addMembers` do `...}).then(function() { // reload member list
  self.findMembers();
});` without `return self.findMembers();`. That means the promise returned by `removeMember`/`addMembers` resolves as soon as the DELETE/PUT succeeds, and any failure in the subsequent reload (`findMembers()` ajax) won’t be propagated to callers (e.g., controller actions can’t wait for or catch it). Since the UI relies on `findMembers()` to refresh `members`, a reload failure can leave stale members displayed with no surfaced error
